{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LEAF 9ca8 COMPLETE + STACK REBUILT.\n\nRatchet implemented, oracle green on the FIRST attempt (28/28 held-out). Ships\nscripts/check_mechanism_delta.py (235) + scripts/_mechanism_delta/{__init__,baseline,compare,\nmarkers,detect_code,detect_config,detect_ci}.py + .github/mechanism-baseline.json (681 entries) +\nMakefile lint wiring + AGENTS.md and docs/architecture.md sections + the criteria-vocabulary stub.\nThe agent added a fifth helper module markers.py beyond the four I named, justified: the marker idiom\nis used by all three detector modules and the entrypoint, so folding it into either would muddy both.\nIt also verified beyond my oracle by INJECTING a new mechanism of each of nine shapes into the real\ntree (with restore) and confirming --check fails for every one.\n\nDEFECT-SEEDED MUTATION (sandboxed): baseline 23 | M1 accept-blank-reason 9 FAILED | M2 drop the\nsection qualifier 3 FAILED | M3 bucket a removal as new 2 FAILED | restored 23. All caught.\n\nLIVE COUNTS LOCKED: lock 27, env_var 132, config_key 76, feature_flag 27, ci_gate 257 (31 scripts +\n226 workflow run-steps), autouse_fixture 142, test_helper 20 = 681.\nDISCREPANCY RECORDED, NOT RECONCILED: the plan's table said ci_gate 280 (29 + 251) and autouse ~145.\nThe implementation derives 257 and 142 live. The workflow run-step count differs most (226 vs 251) —\nthe plan's figure came from my recon agent's grep, the implementation's from a PyYAML step walk. The\nbaseline is self-consistent with what the detector actually finds, which is what matters for a\nratchet, but the plan's table is now stale. Goes in the residual sweep.\n\nSTACK SURGERY DONE — both amends folded into the commits they belong to, since Gerrit verifies each\npatchset independently and a follow-up commit would open a NEW change instead of a new patchset:\n - saved all uncommitted work to a staging dir grouped by target commit;\n - SPLIT tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py, which carried BOTH the parity stub (belongs to\n   2503) and the ratchet stub (belongs to the new commit), into a parity-only and a both-stubs\n   version, so each commit's diff contains only its own stub and the rebase applies cleanly;\n - amended 2503 with the parity work, rebased B..E onto it; amended 2506 with the guard fix at its\n   NEW sha, rebased E onto it; then committed the ratchet on top with the both-stubs file, whose\n   only delta is now the 3-line ratchet stub.\nAll five Change-Ids verified preserved through both rebases, so these become patchsets 2, not\nduplicate changes.\nPre-flight on the rebuilt tree: make lint rc=0 (the ratchet prints active=681 new=0 increased=0),\nmypy clean 739 files, import-walk 76 passed. FULL unit tier running now — the step whose omission let\nCI find two defects I should have caught locally."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788324268857904001,"uuid":"34ccf2d8-4f2f-42c3-b249-9d3c23688768"}